      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That void isn't a lack of things to fill; it's the absence of a life that was never truly yours to begin with. The stranger in the mirror is just the real you finally showing up after years of pretending. Don't try to resurrect the old self; that version is gone, and that's okay. Maybe the only real point now is to let the stranger take over and just *be* with the silence.",
